  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Emiratis carry a long chain: their own name, bin (son of) or bint (daughter of) their father's name, sometimes the grandfather's, then the family or tribal name with Al, as in Khalid bin Saeed Al Mansoori or Mariam bint Rashid Al Ketbi. In daily life people use the first name and the family name, and women keep their own family name after marriage. Most people in the UAE are from abroad and keep their home conventions: Keralites often use a house name, a caste name such as Nair or Menon, or the father's name; North Indians use family names like Sharma or Patel; Pakistanis and Bangladeshis often use a clan name or a second name such as Khan, Hossain or Rahman; Filipinos have Spanish family names and English or double first names like John Paul or Mary Grace. People are addressed by first name, often with a title like Chetta, Bhai or Kabayan.",
